    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0580" n="552" xml:id="pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.5/3–2054</note>
                <head>No. 265<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Counselor (MacArthur) to
                        Harold N. Waddell of the Bureau of Far Eastern Affairs</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d265-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-08-27">August 27, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Attached file.</item>
                </list>
                <p>I have read the attached memorandum from FE recommending a mutual defense treaty
                    with the Republic of China, and while I recognize that a very good case can be
                    made for the conclusion of such an arrangement, I nonetheless have doubts as to
                    the desirability of pursuing such a course at this particular time.</p>
                <p>As a practical matter, I think the various statements which have been made by top
                    officials in this country, including the highest level, have made it quite clear
                    to the Chinese Nationalists, the Chinese Communists, and others, that we would
                    use our military forces to oppose any Chinese Communist attempt to attack
                    Formosa.</p>
                <p>To sum it up, I believe that the considerations which governed the decision with
                    respect to this question last March and April are still valid.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D Mac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d265-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d265-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Secretary Dulles as an attachment to <ref target="#d262">Document
                        262</ref>.</p>
            </note>
